bug_descriptions |bug_id, line_num, content|
    web_render_flex_button_device_width_gate_mismatch_2026-11-28, 0, "Row flex layout (work/webrender-tabbar-20261128, 35d45555c32): plain_button_item is only tag == button and flex_wrap == nowrap, so at k > 1 it routes draw_x through box_x_snap and records box_device_extra_w for ANY <button> flex item with a fractional remainder, including one with an explicit width, flex-grow or min-width. The matching guards are narrower: flex_row_button_label_at_edge needs width auto, flex_grow <= 0 and no min-width, and the button's own reset (layout_with_style tail) is skipped by button_in_flex_row for every plain-row button. So a sized or grown button now keeps a row-recorded device width that no Chrome measurement pins. No Chrome 159 spec covers e.g. <button style=width:80.5px> or flex:1 buttons in a display:flex row at device scale 4."

bugs_active |id, severity, status, title, file, line, reproducible_by, created_at, updated_at, valid|
    web_render_flex_button_device_width_gate_mismatch_2026-11-28, P3, open, "web render: flex-row <button> with explicit width / flex-grow / min-width gets device-width records at k>1 with no Chrome-pinned spec (gates disagree)", src/lib/gc_async_mut/gpu/browser_engine/simple_web_html_layout_renderer_layout_engine.spl, 3965, "display:flex row with <button style=width:80.5px> and <button style=flex:1> at device scale 4; compare border columns with Chrome 159 --force-device-scale-factor=4", 2026-11-28, 2026-11-28, true

bug_investigation_logs |bug_id, line_num, content|
    web_render_flex_button_device_width_gate_mismatch_2026-11-28, 0, "2026-11-28 tabbar lane / Opus review of 35d45555c32: fix options are to give plain_button_item the same width-auto / no-grow / no-min-width conditions, or to measure the sized cases in Chrome and pin them. Existing flex and button specs (26) are green either way."
    web_render_flex_button_device_width_gate_mismatch_2026-11-28, 1, "2026-11-28 button-label-cluster lane: measured in Chrome 159, left OPEN (generic flex-row work, too large for this lane). Page: display:flex;gap:8px;width:390px, buttons Auto | width:80.5px | flex:1 | min-width:90.3px (padding 8px, border 1px #94a3b8). Chrome getBoundingClientRect k=1: 0/45.4219, 53.4219/80.5, 141.9219/149.7813, 299.7031/90.2969; k=4: 0/45.4258, 53.4258/80.5, 141.9258/149.7773, 299.7031/90.2969. Border run starts k=1 Chrome 0 44 53 133 142 291 300 389, Simple 0 44 53 132 141 290 299 389; k=4 Chrome 0 178 214 532 568 1163 1199 1556, Simple 0 178 212 528 564 1160 1196 1556. So Chrome puts the sized, grown and min-width buttons on round(k x exact edge); narrowing plain_button_item (ba32f7509eb) is refuted. A <div> control row with the same boxes is also off (k=1 0 44 53 133 141 291 300 390, k=4 0 176 212 530 564 1164 1200 1557): the 0.42 carry after the auto item and the grown/min-width remainders are dropped by the generic row loop, not only for buttons. The old spec assertion (device-extra-width empty for the grown and min-width buttons) contradicted Chrome and was removed from test/01_unit/browser_engine/button_input_device_width_chrome159_spec.spl."
    web_render_flex_button_device_width_gate_mismatch_2026-11-28, 2, "2026-11-28 Opus review of the button-label-cluster lane (LOW, not introduced): wrap_frac_delta in the wrapped flex row is computed for any <button> with cst.width_px <= 0, which includes the percent-width sentinel (width_px < 0) and ignores max-width. The lane's new k=1 branch reuses that value, so a <button style=width:30%> that ends a wrapped flex line at k=1 now also gets a label-fraction right-edge snap (before, only at k>1 and in the pen). Same gate class as this shard; no Chrome spec covers it. Follow-up: gate on width_px == 0, or pin the percent case in Chrome 159."

